01  – $151,000 </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> $226,002  – $302,000 </td>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>1.25%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> $151,001  and over </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> $302,002  and over </td>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>1.5%</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p class=\"mt-3 text-[0.8125rem] text-ink-soft\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> Only payable without private hospital cover. Family thresholds rise by  <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$1,500</span> for each child after the first. </p>\n<h2 class=\"mt-12 text-xl\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>Study and training loan repayments 2024–25</h2>\n<table class=\"mt-4\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<caption class=\"sr-only\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>Study loan repayment rates for 2024–25</caption>\n<thead data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"col\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>Repayment income</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>Repayment</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> Up to  – $54,434 </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> Nil </td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> $54,435  – $62,850 </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> 1% of total repayment income </td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> $62,851  – $66,620 </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> 2% of total repayment income </td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> $66,621  – $70,618 </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> 3% of total repayment income </td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> $70,619  – $74,855 </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> 3% of total repayment income </td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> $74,856  – $79,346 </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> 4% of total repayment income </td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> $79,347  – $84,107 </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> 4% of total repayment income </td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> $84,108  – $89,154 </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> 5% of total repayment income </td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> $89,155  – $94,503 </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> 5% of total repayment income </td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> $94,504  – $100,174 </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> 6% of total repayment income </td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> $100,175  – $106,185 </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> 6% of total repayment income </td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> $106,186  – $112,556 </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> 7% of total repayment income </td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> $112,557  – $119,309 </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> 7% of total repayment income </td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> $119,310  – $126,467 </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> 8% of total repayment income </td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> $126,468  – $134,056 </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> 8% of total repayment income </td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> $134,057  – $142,100 </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> 9% of total repayment income </td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> $142,101  – $150,626 </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> 9% of total repayment income </td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> $150,627  – $159,663 </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> 10% of total repayment income </td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.8125rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> $159,664  and over </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> 10% of total repayment income </td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p class=\"mt-3 text-[0.8125rem] text-ink-soft\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> Flat system: the rate applies to your whole repayment income. </p>\n<h2 class=\"mt-12 text-xl\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>Offsets and other figures 2024–25</h2>\n<table class=\"mt-4\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<caption class=\"sr-only\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>Offsets and other thresholds for 2024–25</caption>\n<tbody data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> Low income tax offset, maximum </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>$700</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> LITO reduces from </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>$37,500</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> Seniors and pensioners offset, single </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>$2,230</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> Standard deduction (s 25-130) </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> Not available </td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> Super guarantee rate </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>11.5%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> Concessional contributions cap </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>$30,000</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> CGT discount, individuals </th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>50%</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</section></div>\n</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"shell mt-16\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<div class=\"card flex flex-col gap-4 p-6 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<div data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<h2 class=\"text-lg\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>Take the tables with you</h2>\n<p class=\"mt-1 mb-0 max-w-lg text-[0.8125rem] text-ink-soft\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> A one-page PDF of every rate on this page, for all three years. Free to use and share — attribution appreciated but not required. </p>\n</p></div>\n<p> <a href=\"/xyz-accounting-tax-rates.pdf\" class=\"btn btn-secondary shrink-0\" download data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> Download the PDF </a> </div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"shell mt-16\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<div class=\"prose-statement\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>\n<h2 data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>Reading the scale correctly</h2>\n<p data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> The rates are marginal. Moving into a higher bracket taxes only the dollars above the threshold, never the whole income — a pay rise cannot leave you worse off. The  <a href=\"/tax-calculator/\" data-astro-cid-fku4tryq>tax calculator</a> shows the split bracket by bracket on your own income. </p>\n<p data-astro-cid-fku4tryq> Thresholds are not indexed to inflation. They stay fixed until Parliament moves them, which is why wage growth quietly pushes people into higher brackets between reforms. The 2027-28 cut to 14% is already legislated. </p>\n</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"shell mt-20\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-rates-heading\">\n<h2 id=\"faq-rates-heading\" class=\"text-2xl\">Questions people actually ask</h2>\n<dl class=\"mt-6 border-t border-rule\">\n<div class=\"border-b border-rule py-5\">\n<dt class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink\">What are the current Australian tax rates?</dt>\n<dd class=\"m-0 mt-2 max-w-3xl text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft\">For 2026-27: nothing on the first <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$18,200,</span> 15% to <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$45,000,</span> 30% to <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$135,000,</span> 37% to <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$190,000</span> and 45% above that, plus a 2% Medicare levy. The second rate dropped from 16% on 1 July 2026.</dd>\n</p></div>\n<div class=\"border-b border-rule py-5\">\n<dt class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink\">When do the tax rates change again?</dt>\n<dd class=\"m-0 mt-2 max-w-3xl text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft\">The second marginal rate is legislated to fall again to 14% from 1 July 2027. Bracket thresholds themselves are not indexed automatically — they only move when Parliament changes them.</dd>\n</p></div>\n<div class=\"border-b border-rule py-5\">\n<dt class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink\">Which year do I use for my tax return?</dt>\n<dd class=\"m-0 mt-2 max-w-3xl text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft\">The year the income was earned, not the year you lodge. A return lodged now for the year ended 30 June 2026 uses the 2025-26 rates, even though we are in 2026-27.</dd>\n</p></div>\n<div class=\"border-b border-rule py-5\">\n<dt class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink\">Is the Medicare levy included in these rates?</dt>\n<dd class=\"m-0 mt-2 max-w-3xl text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft\">No. The 2% Medicare levy is charged separately on top of the rates in these tables, with a reduction for low incomes. The tax calculator adds it for you.</dd>\n</p></div>\n</dl>\n</section>\n<section class=\"cta-dark\">\n<div class=\"cta-grid\">\n<div>\n<p class=\"band-eyebrow\">Ready to lodge it?</p>\n<h2>A registered agent prepares it, checks it, and lodges it.</h2>\n<p>Most refunds land within two weeks of assessment. The fee is fixed and quoted before we start — nothing is charged until you approve the finished return.</p>\n<div class=\"cta-actions\"> <a href=\"/lodge/\" class=\"btn\">Start your return</a> <a href=\"/pricing/\" class=\"btn btn-secondary\">See pricing</a> </div>\n</p></div>\n<div class=\"cta-spec\">\n<div class=\"cta-spec-row\"><span>Individual returns from</span><b>$99</b></div>\n<div class=\"cta-spec-row\"><span>Registered tax agent</span><b>26233684</b></div>\n<div class=\"cta-spec-row\"><span>Fixed fee, quoted up front</span><i>included</i></div>\n<div class=\"cta-spec-row\"><span>Fee deductible from refund</span><i>included</i></div>\n</p></div>\n</p></div>\n</section>\n</div>\n"
